new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f7d76b3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/figma/inventory-assets.md
@@ -0,0 +1,141 @@
+# Inventory panel: images to export
+
+The inventory panel (`src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/UI/InventoryPanel.luau`) is built
+from the Figma frame **Inventory / Desktop** (node `12:340`) and the **Slot** component set
+(node `20:1`) in `design/figma/inventory-panel.json`. Most of it is drawn with Roblox UI objects.
+This file lists the visuals that are uploaded images instead.
+
+Every id lives in `UI/InventoryAssets.luau` and is the placeholder `rbxassetid://0` for now. After
+uploading an image, paste its id over the placeholder there. Until then the panel draws a stand-in
+in the block's color for each block's art and a text glyph for each icon, and draws nothing for the
+shadow, glow and pattern.
+
+## Export rules for all images
+
+- PNG with a transparent background, exported at **2x**. UI is laid out for a 1080 px tall screen
+  and `Screen.uiScale()` scales it up to 2x on 4K, so 2x stays sharp everywhere. Code draws each
+  image at its 1x size.
+- Roblox shrinks uploads larger than 1024 px on a side. That's why the hexagon pattern is a tile
+  and the shadows are 9-slice images, not full-panel images.
+- **Tinted** images are exported pure white (alpha only), and the code colors them with
+  `ImageColor3` and sets their opacity with `ImageTransparency`. That way the colors stay in code
+  and one upload can be reused.
+
+## Images
+
+| # | Visual | Figma node(s) | Export size (2x) | Drawn at (1x) |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Block art, one per block type (10) | Slot › Content › Block Art (`40:0`, `40:4`, … `40:38`) | 160 × 160 each | 80 × 80 |
+| 2 | Lock icon | Icon/Lock (`40:30`) | 48 × 48 | 24 × 24 |
+| 3 | Close icon | Icon/Close (`40:80`) | 40 × 40 | 20 × 20 |
+| 4 | Hexagon pattern tile | Hex Pattern (`40:78`) | 224 × 384 | tiled at 112 × 192 |
+| 5 | Panel drop shadow (9-slice) | Panel effect `DROP_SHADOW` (`40:88`) | 448 × 448 | stretched to the panel + 32 px on each side |
+| 6 | Selected-slot glow (9-slice) | Slot State=Selected effect `DROP_SHADOW` (`20:3`) | 256 × 256 | 132 × 132 |
+
+### 1. Block art (`InventoryAssets.BlockArt.<Name>`)
+
+The ten block pictures: Brick, Dirt, Grass, Window, Wood, Stone, Sand, Ice, Lamp, Gold. In
+Figma each is an image fill (`scaleMode: FIT`) on a 56 × 56 rectangle with its own drop shadow
+(black 40%, 0 / 4 offset, 8 blur). Roblox has no drop shadow, so **bake the shadow into the
+image**.
+
+- **Export:** an 80 × 80 frame with the 56 × 56 art centered in it (12 px margin on every side),
+  shadow on, background transparent, at 2x: **160 × 160**. The margin holds the shadow, which
+  reaches 4 px above and 12 px below the art.
+- **Roblox:** `ImageLabel`, 80 × 80, at (8, 4) in the 96 × 96 slot (puts the art at (20, 16) as
+  in Figma), `ScaleType = Fit`. In the Locked state `ImageTransparency = 0.6` (the design's 40%
+  content opacity). Not tinted: export in full color.
+- Keys match `BlockTypes` names. A block type with no entry falls back to the color stand-in.
+
+### 2. Lock icon (`InventoryAssets.LockIcon`)
+
+The padlock on locked slots, a white vector.
+
+- **Export:** the 24 × 24 vector frame, pure white, at 2x: **48 × 48**.
+- **Roblox:** `ImageLabel`, 24 × 24, centered at (48, 38) in the slot, `ScaleType = Fit`,
+  `ImageColor3` = Text/Primary `rgb(245, 246, 250)`. Shown only when the slot is locked.
+
+### 3. Close icon (`InventoryAssets.CloseIcon`)
+
+The × in the header's round close button. The 44 × 44 circle behind it (white at 8%) is a
+`TextButton` with a `UICorner`, not part of the image.
+
+- **Export:** the 20 × 20 vector frame, pure white, at 2x: **40 × 40**.
+- **Roblox:** `ImageLabel`, 20 × 20, centered in the button, `ScaleType = Fit`, `ImageColor3` =
+  Text/Primary `rgb(245, 246, 250)`.
+
+### 4. Hexagon pattern tile (`InventoryAssets.HexPatternTile`)
+
+The faint honeycomb behind the panel content: 35 white 112 × 128 hexagon outlines (2 px stroke,
+centered) in rows 96 px apart, every other row moved 56 px right, all in a group at 6% opacity.
+Drawing 35 vectors isn't possible with UI objects, and a full 720 × 380 image would be 1440 × 760
+at 2x and lose detail in Roblox's downscale, so it becomes one seamless repeating tile.
+
+- **Export:** a **112 × 192** frame with clip content on, transparent background, holding the
+  hexagon outlines **at full white opacity** (the 6% is applied in code). The easy way: paste a
+  copy of the whole Hex Pattern group into the frame, set the group to 100% opacity, and move it
+  so the top-left corner of hexagon `40:59` (one in the middle of the pattern, at 768, 526) lands
+  on the frame's (0, 0). The surrounding hexagons then fill the tile, including the parts of
+  strokes that cross its edges. Keep the 2 px centered stroke. Export at 2x: **224 × 384**. Check
+  that it tiles without seams by placing four copies side by side.
+- **Roblox:** `ImageLabel` with `ScaleType = Tile`, `TileSize = 112 × 192`, placed at (−56, −16)
+  from the panel's top-left corner (where the design's first hexagon starts), in a `CanvasGroup`
+  with `GroupTransparency = 0.94` (6% opacity) and a 16 px `UICorner`. The `CanvasGroup` clips
+  the pattern to the rounded corners; `ClipsDescendants` alone only clips to a rectangle.
+
+### 5. Panel drop shadow (`InventoryAssets.PanelShadow`)
+
+The panel's shadow: black 45%, 0 / 12 offset, 32 blur, no spread, under a rounded rectangle
+with a 16 px radius. Roblox can't blur UI, so it's a 9-slice image.
+
+- **Export:** a **224 × 224** frame, transparent, containing a **160 × 160** rectangle with
+  radius 16 at (32, 32). Give the rectangle a black drop shadow at **100%** opacity, 0 / 0
+  offset, 32 blur, 0 spread, with *Show behind transparent areas* on, and set the rectangle's
+  own fill to 0%. The image is only the blurred shadow. Export at 2x: **448 × 448**.
+- **Roblox:** `ImageLabel` behind the panel body, `ScaleType = Slice`,
+  `SliceCenter = Rect(160, 160, 288, 288)`, `SliceScale = 0.5`, size = panel size + 64 × 64,
+  centered on the panel and moved 12 px down, `ImageColor3` black, `ImageTransparency = 0.55`.
+- The slice corners are 80 px (1x) because the corner radius plus the blur reaching in and out
+  (16 + 32 + 32) all needs to stay out of the stretched middle.
+
+### 6. Selected-slot glow (`InventoryAssets.SlotGlow`)
+
+The amber glow around the selected slot: `rgb(255, 200, 60)` at 55%, 0 / 0 offset, 16 blur,
+2 spread, around a 96 × 96 slot with a 12 px radius. The 3 px amber outside stroke is a
+`UIStroke`, not part of the image.
+
+- **Export:** a **128 × 128** frame, transparent, containing a **96 × 96** rectangle with radius
+  14 at (16, 16). The radius is the slot's 12 plus the 2 px spread; the rectangle's size doesn't
+  matter because the 9-slice stretches its middle. Give it a **white** drop shadow at 100%, 0 / 0 offset, 16 blur, 0 spread, *Show behind
+  transparent areas* on, rectangle fill at 0%. Export at 2x: **256 × 256**.
+- **Roblox:** `ImageLabel` behind the slot face, 132 × 132 (the slot + 18 px on each side:
+  16 blur + 2 spread), centered on the slot, `ScaleType = Slice`,
+  `SliceCenter = Rect(96, 96, 160, 160)`, `SliceScale = 0.5`, `ImageColor3 = rgb(255, 200, 60)`,
+  `ImageTransparency = 0.45`. Shown only on the selected slot.
+
+The geometry for 4–6 (`SliceCenter`, `SliceScale`, margins, `TileSize`) is stored next to the ids
+in `InventoryAssets.luau`. If an image is exported at a different size, change both places.
+
+## Built from UI objects, not images
+
+For reference, the rest of the design is built in code and needs no upload:
+
+- Panel fill (`rgb(23, 26, 38)` at 92%), 16 px corners, 2 px inside stroke: `Frame`, `UICorner`,
+  and a `UIStroke` on a frame inset by 2 px (Roblox's `UIStroke` draws outside the edge).
+- Slot background gradient, 12 px corners, 1 px inside stroke and 3 px outside selected stroke:
+  `UIGradient`, `UICorner`, `UIStroke`.
+- Equip button gradient and its 3 px bottom inner shadow: a gradient face that stops 3 px short
+  of the bottom, over the same gradient with a 25% black frame on it.
+- All text in Builder Sans (Medium, Bold, ExtraBold). Text shadows on the title and counts are a
+  black copy of the label moved down 2 px / 1 px.
+
+## Design details Roblox can't reproduce
+
+- **Background blur** on the panel (`BACKGROUND_BLUR`, 24): Roblox UI can't blur what's behind
+  it, and an image can't stand in for a live blur. Left out; the panel is 92% opaque, so it shows
+  little anyway.
+- **Shadow hidden behind the panel** (`showShadowBehindNode: false`): Roblox draws the shadow
+  image under the 8%-transparent panel, so the panel looks very slightly darker than in Figma.
+- **Text shadow blur** on the counts (2 px): the shadow copy is sharp.
+- **Title letter spacing** (+2 px): Roblox text has no tracking setting, so "INVENTORY" is about
+  16 px narrower than in Figma.
